{title: 571 - What Does the Lord Require?}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #571 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 571}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]What does the [Edim]Lord [Am]require [Gm]for [Am/E]praise [Dm]and offering?
[C]What sacrifice, desire [Am/E]or [F]tribute [Am]bid you [C]bring?
[Am]Do justly; [Dm]Love mercy; [F]Walk humbly with [Gm]your [Am]God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Rulers of [Edim]men, [Am]give [Bb]ear! [Gm]Should [Am/E]you [Dm]not justice [Gm]show?
[C]Will God [F]your [Dm]pleading [C]hear, [Am/E]while [F]crime [Am]and cruelty [C]grow?
[Am]Do justly; [Dm]Love mercy; [F]Walk humbly with [Gm]your [Am]God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]How shall our [Edim]life [Am]fulfill [Gm]God's [Am/E]law [Dm]so hard and [Gm]high?
[C]Let Christ [F]endue [Dm]our [C]will [Am/E]with grace [F]to [Am]fortify.
[Am]Then justly, [Dm]in mercy [F]we'll humbly walk [Gm]with [Am]God.
{end_of_verse}
